@akilmakda, I fixed [my previous comment][1]. I meant that #20404 can**not** fix your usecase.
As mentioned in https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/23012#issuecomment-376937241, one fix/work-around I can think of would be to not handle mixed content from the service worker (but that is a change that needs to be made to the SW; it is not something you can do yourself).

[1]: https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/23012#issuecomment-376672174
